;; title: Graphs — A Round Circle
;; desc: (SETPLOT … "EQUAL) gives x and y the same scale, so the circle x² + y² = 4 stays round and its square stays square
;; topic: Maths and curves
;; shows: SETPLOT, GRID, PLOT
SPEED 4
; "EQUAL: one step in x is as long as one step in y.
; The canvas is wider than it is tall, so it shows more of x.
(SETPLOT -3 3 -3 3 "EQUAL)
SETCOLOR 215 210 195        ; light graph paper
GRID 0.5 0.5
SETCOLOR GRAY
AXES 1 1

; Circle with radius 2: x = 2 cos a, y = 2 sin a
SETCOLOR BLUE SETWIDTH 2
PU
FOR "A 0 360 5 [
  PLOT 2 * COS :A 2 * SIN :A
  PD
]

; A square inside it: its corners lie on the circle
MAKE "C SQRT 2              ; 1.41…, because C² + C² = 4
SETCOLOR RED
PU PLOT :C :C
PD PLOT -:C :C
PLOT -:C -:C
PLOT :C -:C
PLOT :C :C
PU HOME HT
